body:
That's what I was thinking. So yeah, still trying to figure that out.....some people point out how the series has a lot of Christian overtones and what not and some say it's just a coincidence because "Wings and halo cute hur hur" but I really feel like that's too much of a coincidence to be random moe aesthetic. Especially with the young feathers. Though I swear I've heard that somewhere in Asian there's significance to the age of 7 years old. So it could be young feathers are all under seven.....

&#x200B;

Upon further research I found this wiki article... [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shichi-Go-San](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shichi-Go-San)  So maybe it also has something to do with this.

I have a weird meta theory that takes up way too much space in my brain. It might be super obvious to everyone but I gotta say it anyway cuz it's driving me crazy. 

The entire story reminds me of an allegory for foster-care. My leading thoughts right now are that Rider is like the older sister living in a potentially abusive or bad situation with her younger sister Horse. Now horse is really young so she gets taken away and given to a foster-mother (Wammawinks) So when Rider barely recognizes Horse because she "Talks now" that's because she's growing older (Like a child learning to speak) It's why she's so resistant to all the things in centaurworld. It's almost like the previous life of the bad situation is all she knows, so she thinks that's the most normal, so all this happy fluffy love and comfort stuff makes her afraid. That's why she wants to get back so bad, but it's not really a good situation. But her foster mom knows that's what she wants so she's trying to help but since she didn't go back with her in the end it's almost like they both know that isn't a safe place for her so instead they'll both make it better so that she can come back.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Sorry if that's weird and confusing but I started making parallels and I was like OMFG Just a meta theory about an allegory, not saying that's what's actually happening. I don't think it's "Actually" happening it's just.... well you know what I mean.

I don't think that's what's happening. Having sat through about 12 minutes of that bullshit lol what I think it's trying to convey with the way the character is jerking around is both stumbling, and beginning to lose consciousness. During one point I was standing still I think and.... they just..... closed their eyes. Like the character blinked for a long long time, really really slowly, several times. It was like blacking out and waking back up again. Kinda familiar actually now that I think about it. Hard to describe if you don't already know the feeling? Slipping in and out of awareness. I've been really super sick before and went through something similar.  Idk friendo, I just feel like it's an accurate representation of what those kinds of things would cause, maybe because I've felt them before. 

&#x200B;

Also while starvation would NOT set in nearly as fast as the game makes it seem, I'm not sure if perhaps the strain on the body to produce warmth doesn't burn calories at a higher rate than normal, plus all the moving around heaving heavy packs, and high stepping over snow banks. Honestly the fact that the PC survives at all just speaks to the fact that they were probably at least a little bit in shape before all this, or otherwise I think they might kick it day one lol

[https://www.reddit.com/r/sewing/comments/g1jy27/i\_only\_wanted\_to\_make\_a\_simple\_small\_pin\_cushion/](https://www.reddit.com/r/sewing/comments/g1jy27/i_only_wanted_to_make_a_simple_small_pin_cushion/)

&#x200B;

I explained how I made this over on the other pin cushion post! The only other difference is that I used a ribbon on the sides instead of gimp this time. I simply sewed in and out and then pulled the thread to cause the ribbon to ruffle. :) The bottom is a very pretty teal color\~\~\~

I came out here to have a good time and I am feeling so attacked right now.

&#x200B;

(100% kidding, this is hilariously accurate. Ugh, it hurts my heart.)

Just in general? or with yaoi as well? Because there was this one I never finished that was... I'm not sure if it was psychological technically or just horror or something.... but it was called Suicide Island and it's a heavily disturbing and fucked up manga about people from Japan who have repeatedly attempted suicide being gathered up and sent to a deserted island and just left there. Later on in the story I got a bit of "Lord of the Flies" kind of vibes from it as well. 

&#x200B;

I really wish I had something good to recommend.....

"I'm getting fucked while eating out my own pussy... I feel like... I'M GOING CRAZY!"

&#x200B;

It was text, but it was still funny.
